From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:41:21 -0400
Subject: [SkPath] Increase GenerationID to 64 bits

* GenerationID was originally intended to be a modification tracker per object but became conflated with global uniqueness. This was fine so long as ID usages were sufficiently temporally separated that wrapping IDs would never collide. However, at 32 bits it is feasible for an attacker to cause wrapping in a relatively small amount of time.

* This patch ups the GenerationID to 64 bits

Bug: b/562038679
Bug: b/556268833
Change-Id: I12d2e93cc32c8922fe0b19a1f737e6196ed54dd8
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1366216
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>

